course: dictionary
lesson: 14911
title: Redeemable: swapped or saved
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Redeemable is an adjective, so it describes a thing or a person. The ending -able means "able to be", so redeemable means able to be redeemed, or swapped for something.
explain: Shops use this idea every day. «Your voucher is redeemable at any shop in town until Friday.» You can swap the voucher for goods or a prize, so redeemable means it can be exchanged. Check it with the swap test: can I swap this for something? Yes, so the meaning fits.
explain: The word can also mean able to be saved or made good again. «The villain in the story is still redeemable.» The clue is that he might change and become good. Here redeemable means "able to be saved", not "already fixed".
fact: Redeemable is an adjective: it describes a thing or a person.
fact: «Redeemable» means able to be exchanged for money, goods or a prize.
fact: «Redeemable» can also mean able to be saved or made good again.
fact: «Not redeemable for cash» means you cannot swap it for money.
fact: In churches, Christians believe every person is redeemable, able to be saved by God's grace.
exercise: «Your voucher is redeemable at any shop in town.» What does redeemable mean here? | *Can be exchanged for goods | Is old and out of date | Is torn and cannot be used | Can be sold for a lot of money
exercise: «The villain in the story is still redeemable.» What does redeemable suggest? | Hidden under the bed | *Able to be saved or made good again | Very rich and powerful | Impossible to change
exercise: «This coupon is not redeemable for cash.» What does this tell you? | You can swap it for money at any bank | *You cannot swap it for money | It is worth more than money | It is a kind of cash
test: «This token is redeemable for a free ice cream.» Which meaning fits best? | Can be eaten at night | *Can be swapped for a prize | Can be lost easily | Can be sung loudly
test: Christians believe every person is redeemable. What does this mean? | *Every person can be saved by God's grace | Every person must be quiet in church | Every person is rich | No person can ever change
exam: Which sentence uses redeemable correctly? | «The sky is redeemable as a noisy tune.» | *«The old coupon is still redeemable until next week.» | «My bike is redeemable with a big, loud bell.» | «The cat was redeemable under the table.»
